Circuit Lab
===========

Circuit Lab is built on two MIT-licensed projects. Their notices are kept here
and in the app's Credits panel.

1. ohmlet — https://github.com/JENW1N/ohmlet
   The base of this folder: the app shell, 3D breadboards and parts, wire
   routing, render modes, the MNA circuit solver, behavioural chips, the
   validator and their tests. Its licence is in ./LICENSE:

   MIT License — Copyright (c) 2026 JENW1N

   Circuit Lab changes: the microcontroller boards and the parts that need
   them, the Code / Lessons / Credits / How-to-play UI, the AI panel switched
   off (no model key in the browser), storage keys renamed, framing tweaks.

2. OpenCircuit 3D — https://github.com/gabrieleviolait/opencircuit
   The microcontroller side was ported from it and rebuilt for ohmlet's chip
   bridge: the avr8js board runner (src/mcu/avr/runtime.ts), the fast Arduino
   runtime (src/mcu/fast/*), the in-browser compile flow through a blob
   worker (src/mcu/avr/compile.ts), the display / NeoPixel / servo / sensor
   helpers (src/sim/chips/peripherals.ts) and the lesson presets
   (src/lessons/presets.ts).

